// aug17d hz1 divergence_000000 (2026-08-18): a ~40% per-run compile
// flap — `#[tail_recursive]` on a genuinely tail-recursive lambda
// failed with "recurses through a non-tail self-call or mutual
// recursion", landing on EITHER engine (interp locally, jit on hz1),
// so the oracle saw CompileErr vs value. Root cause in
// `analysis::strongly_connected` phase 2 (Kosaraju): the reverse walk
// claimed nodes with `components.insert(..).is_some()`, which
// OVERWRITES an already-claimed node's label before noticing the
// claim — a plain caller was folded into its callee's component, the
// callee's SCC read size 2, `only_self` failed, and the def's
// RecursionKind summary froze at Recursive. Which of the two twin rec
// lambdas got folded depended on hash iteration order of the DFS
// roots. Fixed: an already-claimed node is a barrier
// (`contains_key` first — the first claim, made under a later finish
// time, IS its SCC). The mislabel also marked the plain caller→callee
// call site as a recursive edge.
{let a = array::init(i64:1, |x: i64| -> i64 {let rec lp = |n: i64, acc: i64| -> i64 select n {i64:0 => acc, _ => lp(n - i64:1, i64:1 + n)}; lp(i64:500, i64:7) + {#[tail_recursive]
let rec f = |n: i64, acc: i64| -> i64 select n {i64:0 => acc, _ => f(n - i64:1, acc + n)}; f(i64:10, i64:0)}}); array::fold(a, i64:0, |acc, x| acc + x)}
